{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The plain of the Jordan.</b> A place of vegetation, and the kaf is doubled, or it is missing — \"a broad plain\" (Isaiah 30:23). And likewise bat ein, from \"the pupil of his eye\" (Zechariah 2:12)." "<b>Irrigated.</b> Masculine after feminine, and likewise \"fire not blown shall consume him\" (Job 20:26)." "<b>Before YHWH destroyed.</b> Before it was destroyed; and it is a verb from the heavy binyan with dagesh."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "The point is that משקה has masculine form despite deriving from a feminine root or pattern; the Job parallel similarly pairs a grammatical gender mismatch."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:28.995283017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}